    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task: on successful owner creation, enqueue a welcome notification via the logger named `NOTIFY`, carrying the owner id and memberId.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New function class** \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java` (in `rest/function/owner/`). A small, single-responsibility step that reads the persisted `Owner` via `@Val` and emits one line to the `NOTIFY` logger with the owner id and member id. It mirrors the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern (dedicated named logger, `@Val Owner`) rather than duplicating that class's audit logic.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted an `enqueueWelcome` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `audit` and `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance. Placing it after `save`/`audit` guarantees the generated id and assigned member id are populated.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes (it asserts a NOTIFY line contains both the returned owner id and memberId), and all 6 tests remain green.",
